the final stretch before election day  and both president trump  and joe biden are spending time on the  campaign trail until the very last  moment  our washington correspondent alexandra  limon joining us now live in wilmington  delaware and  alex tell us how the democratic nominee  joe biden  spent his day and what the strategy is  for him on this final day before  election day  hey good evening well here in wilmington  delaware is where joe biden is expected  to make his election night speech  tomorrow night but today he did spend  the entire day on the campaign trail  starting off with a rally  in ohio and then he moved on to have  actually multiple  events in the state of pennsylvania and  it wasn't just joe biden it was his  running mate kamala harris also his wife  dr jill biden and other members of the  biden team  that just fanned out across the entire  state of pennsylvania  there's a couple of reasons for that  strategy wise number one they want to  get the message out to every single  voter  that their vote absolutely matters and  if they didn't vote early  they should get to the polls and try to  vote in in a safe way tomorrow  but number two pennsylvania is very much  up for grabs for either candidate  president trump or joe biden and there  are 20 electoral votes at stake  and president trump won by a very very  thin margin  in 2016 not just in pennsylvania but  michigan wisconsin  and so that's why biden is focusing on  the midwest  and also on pennsylvania and as you  mentioned pennsylvania and michigan both  key battleground states in the race for  president  but there are also states that we may  not know the results of on election  night  can you walk our viewers through why  yeah definitely you know every single  state has their own election laws and  other states like florida for example  that are also up for grabs very tight  race there  they can begin to count those mail-in  and absentee ballots  weeks ahead of time that is not the case  in pennsylvania or  in michigan those states cannot begin  counting until  election day and there are just  thousands of ballots that have been  pouring in  by mail because of the pandemic so the  election officials in those states say  it could take several days  perhaps as long as friday to get their  ballots counted and their results  finalized but i should mention this is  completely normal we see things like  this happen  every single election in one state or  another it happened in 2016.  they're just asking for some patience  while they get those ballots counted  we all probably can use a little  patience these days thank you so much  alexandra limon joining us tonight  from delaware we do appreciate your time  and thank you
 

